[0.001, "o", "\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[27d\u001b[37m\u001b[44mCards: \u001b[30m\u001b[47mA\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m3\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m4\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m5\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m10\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47mJ\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47mK\u001b[37m\u001b[44m\u001b[41X\u001b[27;63H37 cards in deck  \u001b[28;64H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K I have 6 cards  \u001b[29d\b"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K\u001b[30d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K\u001b[28d\b\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\u001b[9dThis is the traditional children's card game \"Go Fish\". We each get\r\u001b[10d"]
[0.000, "o", "seven cards, and the rest of the deck is kept to be drawn from later. The\r\u001b[11dobject of the game is to collect \"books\", or all of the cards of a single\r\u001b[12d"]
[0.000, "o", "value. For example, getting four 2's would give you a \"book of 2's\".\r\u001b[14dWe take turns asking each other for cards, but you can only ask me for\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "a card value you already have. If I have any, I must give them to you,\r\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "and you can keep asking. If you ask me for a card value I don't have,\r\u001b[17dthen I'll tell you to \"Go Fish!\", which means that you draw a card from\r\u001b[18d"]
[0.000, "o", "the deck. If you draw the card you asked me for, you get to keep asking\r\u001b[19d"]
[0.000, "o", "me for cards. If not, then it's my turn. The game stops when one of us\r\u001b[20d"]
[0.000, "o", "runs out of cards, and the winner is the one with the most books.\r\u001b[22dYou ask for a card by typing its name (a234567891jqk), type x to quit,\r\u001b[24d"]
[0.000, "o", "I get to start.\r\u001b[25d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;1mI ask you for 2. You say \"GO FISH!\"\r\u001b[26d\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
